TI  - Role of AI Chatbots in Enhancing Financial Literacy among Women Entrepreneurs in the Digital Era
AB  - The emergence of Artificial Intelligence (AI) has transformed the delivery of financial services and created new opportunities for enhancing financial literacy through intelligent digital platforms. Among these innovations, AI chatbots have gained considerable attention for their ability to provide real-time financial guidance, personalized support, and interactive learning experiences. This study investigates the role of AI chatbots in enhancing financial literacy among women entrepreneurs in the digital era. The study aims to examine the influence of AI chatbot accessibility, ease of use, financial knowledge improvement, digital financial awareness, and financial decision-making ability on overall financial literacy. A descriptive and analytical research design was adopted for the study. Primary data were collected from 320 women entrepreneurs using a structured questionnaire based on a five-point Likert scale. Statistical tools including descriptive analysis, reliability analysis, KMO and Bartlett’s Test, factor analysis, correlation analysis, and multiple regression analysis were employed using SPSS Version 29. The findings reveal that AI chatbot technologies significantly contribute to improving financial knowledge, digital financial awareness, entrepreneurial confidence, and financial decision-making ability among women entrepreneurs. The correlation and regression results indicate strong positive relationships between AI chatbot-related factors and overall financial literacy. The study further confirms that AI chatbots serve as effective digital financial learning tools that promote financial inclusion and entrepreneurial empowerment. The study concludes that AI-enabled conversational technologies can play a transformative role in strengthening financial literacy and supporting sustainable entrepreneurial development among women entrepreneurs in the rapidly evolving digital economy.
